          "title": "5. Walk the Orbit: Generate Retrograde Yourself",
          "description": "Stand on the circle marked on the floor \u2014 this is Earth's orbit. A stationary Mars floats several feet ahead against the distant stars. Walk slowly around the circle, keeping your gaze on Mars. As you pass the point of closest approach, watch Mars appear to slide backward against the constellations. Complete the full loop to personally produce the retrograde pattern with your own motion. Detect the closest-approach marker to continue."
        },
